2026-09-03T11:29Z UPSTREAM MOVED UNDER THIS TRACKER THE MORNING IT WAS FILED. Issue #48 closed 2026-09-03T07:59Z with the maintainer implementing all four requests on main for the next release, and item 2 is gap 3's substance: a build whose embedder gave up is now unfinished, keeps its checkpoint and withholds the library version stamp so action:update falls back to the resuming build; and a resumed build asks the store for committed passages carrying no vector, 500 at a time, and buys exactly those. Items already crawled are not re-fetched, bodies already read are not re-read, passages already embedded are not re-embedded. That is the non-destructive resume this tracker records as required by R3 and R4, and it is the mechanism this repository proposed in its #48 comment of 2026-09-02 -- one query on the existing nullable passages.vector column. Item 4 adds passagesWithoutVectors and a measured embedRate to status, which is coverage honesty rather than the work.stage.trigger.outcome counters R3 and R13 read, so this rung's four counter-blocked cells are NOT unblocked by it. Nothing here is measured: main is not the reviewed SHA, every cell in the matrix was taken against b05ed69 (v1.12.0), and this entry records that the baseline moved, not that anything passes. Re-derive before arguing, as 0033 already says.
2026-09-03T11:34Z GAP 3 IS CLOSED UPSTREAM, VERIFIED IN SOURCE RATHER THAN FROM THE MAINTAINER'S SUMMARY, and it shipped in v1.13.0 today rather than merely landing on main as the previous entry said. Three reads. sqlite-index.ts prepares unembedded as SELECT id, item_key, title, text, source FROM passages WHERE vector IS NULL ORDER BY pid LIMIT ? -- the exact mechanism this repository proposed in its #48 comment, one query on the existing nullable column. build.ts's unembeddedNotice tells the user that action:build RESUMES, embedding exactly those passages and re-fetching nothing, and warns against action:refresh which pays for every vector a second time. And StartBuildOptions carries fresh?: boolean with the comment that action:build deliberately does not set it, because throwing away work already committed and paid for is the complaint behind #24; resume is deliberately not keyed on the version stamp, since a stopped build has none by design. The release commit chore(release): 1.13.0 is newer than the issue-48 merge, so this is released code, not a branch. What is NOT established by that reading: whether a build stopped by the PAUSE verb resumes the same way. The machinery keys on committed passages carrying no vector plus the crawl checkpoint rather than on why the build stopped, which suggests it does, but the notice's re-fetching-nothing claim is written about the embedder-died case and nobody has driven the pause path. That is this tracker's remaining question on R3, and it needs the v1.13.0 re-baseline before it can be asked at all.
